// Test: dylib-missing-errors
// Purpose: a lazy-dylib module that cannot be loaded must fail loudly at
//          load time (issue #281) — the diagnostic must name the module, the
//          exact file it tried, why it failed, and how to build it. Never a
//          generic "unknown C function" line, and never (as before #294's
//          first half) silent degradation into an arena abort. The
//          external fn declaration passes typecheck; run_crash_tests.sh
//          supplies three sandboxed lib/ states (file absent / dylib without
//          vm_load_self / dylib that does not provide the function) and
//          asserts stderr + exit code for each. stdout must stay empty.
external fn nodyslib.thing(x: int) -> int

fn main() {
  print(nodyslib.thing(1))
}